url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2019-10-04T14:01:17Z","updated_at":"2019-10-04T14:01:17Z","body":"you're only creating two Teacher objects which means for there to be more, something is being loaded, and since there are no queries shown, it has to be related to expiration.   i'll look in a few but I would suppose if you put expire_on_commit=False in your session that might change this behavior.    not like that's the solution but it would confirm this has something to do with refreshing collections.    also I'm wondering (again I will know in 3 seconds when I run the script) if the list remains in the wrong state if you do only a flush(), and not a commit(), at the end, or if this is only seen within the after flush handler itself.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/issues/comments/538409718/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"zzzeek","id":128223,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyODIyMw==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/128223?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek","html_url":"https://github.com/zzzeek","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/issues/comments/538410970","html_url":"https://github.com/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/issues/4890#issuecomment-538410970","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/issues/4890","id":538410970,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDUzODQxMDk3MA==","user":{"login":"maarten-dp","id":35668288,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM1NjY4Mjg4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/35668288?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/maarten-dp","html_url":"https://github.com/maarten-dp","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maarten-dp/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maarten-dp/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maarten-dp/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maarten-dp/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maarten-dp/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maarten-dp/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maarten-dp/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maarten-dp/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maarten-dp/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2019-10-04T14:04:04Z","updated_at":"2019-10-04T14:04:04Z","body":"expire_on_commit=False does indeed result in the correct behavior :)","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/issues/comments/538410970/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"maarten-dp","id":35668288,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM1NjY4Mjg4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/35668288?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/maarten-dp","html_url":"https://github.com/maarten-dp","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maarten-dp/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maarten-dp/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maarten-dp/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maarten-dp/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maarten-dp/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maarten-dp/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maarten-dp/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maarten-dp/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/maarten-dp/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/issues/comments/538429029","html_url":"https://github.com/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/issues/4890#issuecomment-538429029","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/issues/4890","id":538429029,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDUzODQyOTAyOQ==","user":{"login":"zzzeek","id":128223,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyODIyMw==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/128223?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek","html_url":"https://github.com/zzzeek","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2019-10-04T14:48:30Z","updated_at":"2019-10-04T14:48:30Z","body":"There was an issue in openstack neutron that might have been similar to this, where we saw multiple objects with the same identity popping up as a result of events.\r\n\r\nI'm trying to see if I can add a warning (Python warning) for this as it is likely the best I can do, however this condition is also known for other reasons where the warning might not work there so need to see.\r\n\r\nat the very least we probably need a dragon at https://docs.sqlalchemy.org/en/13/orm/events.html?highlight=after_flush#sqlalchemy.orm.events.SessionEvents.after_flush .\r\nbasically the after_flush() event is before the Session has done the work of putting the new objects into the identity map, or done anything with clearing out the pending history of collections.   The new Class and Teacher objects are not in the identity map yet, but the rows have been inserted into the database.   \r\n\r\nso when you emit a load of target.classes and then each teacher object, which is what target.students does, it goes to the database, gets primary key 1 and 2 for the classes / teachers, puts the newly loaded class / teacher objects into the identity map, and populates the collection.  then it also gives you the objects that you have appended to the target.classes collection which are still sitting in a temporary buffer (see this via `inspect(target)._pending_mutations[\"classes\"].added_items`) also, which is this other Class object that also has primary key 2 because its row was just inserted, but is in the middle of a flush and is not in the identity map yet.\r\n\r\nthe end result is nothing is really corrupted since the identity map has maintained just two Class and Teacher objects but your collection is in an invalid state due to where it was loaded.\r\n\r\nthis is a patch that I can't put in as is, as we have an existing test where this is a valid condition (swapping primary keys of objects), although I can decide that the warning is worth it in that case also.  if you wanted to play with this patch to see the warning that might be helpfu.\r\n\r\n```diff\r\ndiff --git a/lib/sqlalchemy/orm/identity.py b/lib/sqlalchemy/orm/identity.py\r\nindex 2da5d66b3..cb49e1719 100644\r\n--- a/lib/sqlalchemy/orm/identity.py\r\n+++ b/lib/sqlalchemy/orm/identity.py\r\n@@ -125,10 +125,13 @@ class WeakInstanceDict(IdentityMap):\r\n                 if existing is not state:\r\n                     self._manage_removed_state(existing)\r\n                 else:\r\n-                    return\r\n+                    return None\r\n+        else:\r\n+            existing = None\r\n \r\n         self._dict[state.key] = state\r\n         self._manage_incoming_state(state)\r\n+        return existing\r\n \r\n     def add(self, state):\r\n         key = state.key\r\ndiff --git a/lib/sqlalchemy/orm/session.py b/lib/sqlalchemy/orm/session.py\r\nindex c345c4281..a2801fcea 100644\r\n--- a/lib/sqlalchemy/orm/session.py\r\n+++ b/lib/sqlalchemy/orm/session.py\r\n@@ -1935,7 +1935,13 @@ class Session(_SessionClassMethods):\r\n                 # there can be an existing state in the identity map\r\n                 # that is replaced when the primary keys of two instances\r\n                 # are swapped; see test/orm/test_naturalpks.py -> test_reverse\r\n-                self.identity_map.replace(state)\r\n+                old = self.identity_map.replace(state)\r\n+                if old is not None:\r\n+                    util.warn(\r\n+                        \"Identity map already had an identity for %s, \"\r\n+                        \"replacing it with newly flushed object\"\r\n+                        % (instance_key, )\r\n+                    )\r\n                 state._orphaned_outside_of_session = False\r\n \r\n         statelib.InstanceState._commit_all_states(\r\n\r\n```\r\n\r\n","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/issues/comments/538429029/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"zzzeek","id":128223,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyODIyMw==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/128223?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek","html_url":"https://github.com/zzzeek","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/issues/comments/538440782","html_url":"https://github.com/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/issues/4890#issuecomment-538440782","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/issues/4890","id":538440782,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDUzODQ0MDc4Mg==","user":{"login":"sqla-tester","id":8250554,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgyNTA1NTQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8250554?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqla-tester","html_url":"https://github.com/sqla-tester","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqla-te